 one position, so a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keyed by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Edges.Index"},{"type":"text","text":" (a weight) is the same in both directions. Positions are valid until the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph is mutated."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Counting."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Neighborhoods count edge ends. A vertex ","type":"text"},{"code":"w ≠ v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" appears in ","type":"text"},{"code":"neighbors(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once per edge between them. A self-loop has both its ends at ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" appears in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"neighbors(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" twice per loop, and the loop’s position twice in ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"adjacency_list","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", LEMON, igraph). ","type":"text"},{"code":"degree(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the length of either, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop counts 2 and the degrees sum to ","type":"text"},{"code":"2 * edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertex and edge indices.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" As for ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": with ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" maps the vertices one-to-one onto ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives adjacency in index space. A representation with dense edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indices also reports ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and then ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" maps edge positions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one-to-one onto ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<edgeIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"edge_index","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", petgraph’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"EdgeIndexable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms that mark edges (bridges, cut vertices, Euler tours) keep that state in arrays too.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdgeIndices(ofIndex:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists them parallel to ","type":"text"},{"code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Laws.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Every conformer satisfies:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexCount == vertices.count"},{"text":", the vertices are distinct, and every edge’s endpoints are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeCount == edges.count"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For every vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the position of each edge with an end at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" once per end (a self-loop twice); each such edge has "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" as an endpoint;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"oppositeVertex(to: v, acrossEdgeAt: e)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[e].oppositeVertex(to: v)"},{"type":"text","text":";"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighbors(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the opposite vertices in the same order; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"degree(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"count."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The degrees sum to ","type":"text"},{"code":"2 * edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"contains(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is true exactly for the edges in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in either orientation, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"contains","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is false (and does not trap) for anything","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"absent.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Asking again gives the same answer."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"With vertex indices, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" is in index order: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex(atIndex: i)"},{"text":" is the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"text":"th vertex.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With vertex indices, "},{"code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: vertexIndex(of: v))","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"neighbors(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mapped through "},{"code":"vertexIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", in the sa